  "term": "glucose",
  "definition": "Glucose, specifically regular D-glucose in this context, is a substance whose metabolism in the brain can be measured with certain MRI methods. Tracking glucose metabolism may help identify disease-related changes and monitor responses to treatment in neurological research.",
